# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository, and checked out as LF
# everywhere. Without this, an editor writing CRLF turns an ordinary edit into
# a whole-file rewrite: one commit here landed as +1945/-1142 when the real
# change was ~300 lines, which also sends git blame for every line in those
# files to the wrong commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never normalize these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.db   binary
*.key  binary
